    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "gold and silver are obvious, but i'm worried about the immediate chaos when the screens go dark. if the banks are executing this, they'll likely freeze all electronic transfers and digital accounts first to prevent a run. how do we handle the first 48-72 hours of the transition when nobody can access their liquid assets? what's the specific strategy for maintaining liquidity without the digital grid?",
